Chapter: LinearBasic
  cites Codex chapter General

 A value typed `linear X` must be used exactly once. The linearity
 checker should accept `use-once` (consumes) but reject `use-twice`.

Section: Definitions

  consume : linear Integer -> Integer
  consume (n) = n * 2

  use-once : Integer
  use-once = consume 21

  opening : Integer = use-once

